{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.rowFactor_addBoxRow_row_above_short","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.rowFactor_addBoxRow_row_above_short","kind":"theorem","line":583,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L583-L595","doc":"**Rows above the new box that the box's column misses.** If row `i` is no\nlonger than `λ_r` the changed column lies outside it, so the factor is equal\noutright — no surgery, and no nonvanishing hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.rowFactor_addBoxRow_row_above","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.rowFactor_addBoxRow_row_above","kind":"theorem","line":564,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L564-L581","doc":"**Rows above the new box, when the box's column meets them.** Exactly one\ncell of the row — the one in column `λ_r` — has its hook raised, so the two row\nfactors differ by swapping that single factor.\n\nThis is the third and last case, and the only one needing product surgery: below\nthe box nothing moves, and the receiving row splits off its new cell by\n`List.range_succ`, but here the changed cell sits in the *interior* of the\nrow's range. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.rowFactor_addBoxRow_same_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.rowFactor_addBoxRow_same_row","kind":"theorem","line":519,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L519-L540","doc":"**The row that received the box.** Its factor is the old row's cells with\nevery hook raised by one, times the factor of the new cell.\n\n`List.range_succ` is what makes this a clean split: the new row's index range is\nthe old one with `λ_r` appended, so the product splits as a product over the old\ncells and a single new factor. The old cells are then rewritten one at a time by\nthe arm-growth half of the update rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.rowFactor_addBoxRow_row_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.rowFactor_addBoxRow_row_below","kind":"theorem","line":508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L508-L517","doc":"**Rows below the new box contribute the same factor.** Neither the row's\nlength nor any of its hook lengths moved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_eq_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_eq_prod","kind":"theorem","line":473,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L473-L493","doc":"**`schurElement` is a product over cells.** The prefactor `Q^{n(λ)}` times\nthe product over rows of the product over that row's cells.\n\nThis is the form every step of (P) is stated against: adding a box changes the\nhook length of finitely many cells and adds one new one, so the ratio of two\nSchur elements is a ratio of two products differing on a known set — a statement\none can make about a product and cannot make about a fold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.rowFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.rowFactor","kind":"def","line":469,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L469-L471","doc":"The factor row `i` contributes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.cellFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.cellFactor","kind":"def","line":463,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L463-L467","doc":"The factor cell `(i, j)` contributes: content numerator over hook\ndenominator. Note the hook length is taken **in `lam`** — this is the quantity\nthe box-addition update rule (`QPartitionCombinatorics`) moves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.substrate_not_tl_degenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.substrate_not_tl_degenerate","kind":"theorem","line":431,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L431-L441","doc":"**The substrate never lands on a TL wall of any partition\n(sorry-free).**  Packaging `substrate_avoids_tl_locus` against\n`schurElement_tl_eq_zero_iff`: for $Q > 1$, $X \\le 0$ and any\n$\\lambda$, if the level-$N$ vanishing criterion held then $X$ would\nequal the positive wall $Q^{-N}$, contradicting $X \\le 0$.  So no\ncontent level can degenerate the Schur element at the substrate —\nthe semisimple-stratum reason behind `schurElement_ne_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.substrate_avoids_tl_locus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.substrate_avoids_tl_locus","kind":"theorem","line":416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L416-L429","doc":"**The substrate regime lies strictly outside the TL degeneracy\nlocus (sorry-free).**  Every Temperley--Lieb wall sits at a\n*positive* Markov parameter $X = Q^{-N}$ (since $Q > 1 \\Rightarrow\nQ^{-N} > 0$), whereas the physical substrate regime is $X \\le 0$.\nHence at the substrate no content level $N$ can place $X$ on a wall:\n$X \\ne Q^{-N}$ for every $N$.  This is the structural reason\n`schurElement_ne_zero` holds for *all* $\\lambda$ at $X \\le 0$ — the\nvanishing criterion `schurElement_tl_eq_zero_iff` can never fire, so\nthe substrate sits in the semisimple stratum away from every\nlevel-rank wall. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_tl_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_tl_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":401,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L401-L414","doc":"**The Temperley--Lieb stratification (sorry-free iff).**  At the\nphysical Markov parameter $X = Q^{-N}$, $Q > 1$, the Schur element\nof $\\lambda$ vanishes **iff** $\\lambda$ contains a cell of content\n$N$.  Combined with the cited `SchurElementCriterion`, this locates\nthe semisimplicity boundary exactly: the level-rank / TL quotient\nis cut out by the content-$N$ hyperplane of the cell lattice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_tl_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_tl_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":382,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L382-L399","doc":"**TL non-vanishing (sorry-free).**  With no content-$N$ cell, the\nSchur element at $X = Q^{-N}$ survives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_tl_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_tl_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":367,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L367-L380","doc":"**TL vanishing (sorry-free).**  A content-$N$ cell kills the Schur\nelement at $X = Q^{-N}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.tl_numerator_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.tl_numerator_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L351-L365","doc":"At $X = Q^{-N}$ the content numerator vanishes exactly at content\n$c = N$ (sorry-free): $1 - Q^{-N} Q^{c} = 0 \\iff c = N$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.HasContentCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.HasContentCell","kind":"def","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L309-L311","doc":"`lam` contains an in-range cell of content `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.semisimple_of_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.semisimple_of_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L261-L271","doc":"**Semisimplicity at every rank in the substrate regime (sorry-free\nmodulo the cited criterion).**  For $Q > 1$, $X \\leq 0$: every rank\nis semisimple, with the Schur-element leg *computed*, not assumed.\nThis is the Schur-theoretic discharge of the `WenzlCriterion`\nhypothesis of `QOU.Information.PNeqNpEquivalence` — the two cited\nclasses state the same literature theorem from two equivalent\nangles (parameter genericity vs. Schur-element non-vanishing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.SchurElementCriterion.semisimple_of_schur_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.SchurElementCriterion.semisimple_of_schur_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L256-L256","doc":"Schur-element non-vanishing implies semisimplicity, carried as a\nhypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.SchurElementCriterion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.SchurElementCriterion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L253-L253","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.SchurElementCriterion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.SchurElementCriterion","kind":"class","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L245-L259","doc":"**Cited Geck--Pfeiffer criterion** (hypothesis class, not a theorem\nof this development): if every Schur element at rank $n$ is\nnonzero, the algebra is semisimple at rank $n$.  `semisimple n` is\nan opaque per-rank `Prop`; **no instance is declared** — the\nsymmetrizing-trace theory is not in Mathlib, and a fabricated\ninstance would launder [geckpfeiffer2000] into a Lean proof.\n\nRef: [geckpfeiffer2000] Geck--Pfeiffer, Thm 7.2.6. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L224-L243","doc":"**Schur-element non-vanishing at the substrate regime\n(sorry-free).**  For $Q > 1$ and $X \\leq 0$, every Wenzl Schur\nelement is nonzero: every content numerator is positive, every hook\ndenominator is strictly negative (hook lengths are positive), and\nthe prefactor $Q^{n(\\lambda)}$ is a nonzero power of a positive\nreal.  This is the computational heart of Wenzl semisimplicity,\nproved on the concrete `schurElement`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.one_sub_mul_zpow_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.one_sub_mul_zpow_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L212-L222","doc":"For $Q > 0$, $X \\leq 0$ the content numerator $1 - X\\,Q^{c}$ is\nnonzero (indeed positive) at every content $c \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\n(sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.one_sub_pow_ne_zero_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.one_sub_pow_ne_zero_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L206-L210","doc":"For $Q > 1$ the hook denominator $1 - Q^{h}$ is nonzero at every\npositive hook length (sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.hookLength_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.hookLength_pos","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L173-L183","doc":"In-range cells have positive hook length (sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.wenzlNormalisation_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.wenzlNormalisation_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L132-L150","doc":"**Connection theorem** — y_λ is well-defined for `Q ≠ 1`,\n`X ≠ 1`, since the denominator `Z_n = ((1−X)/(1−Q))^n` is then\nnonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.jonesMarkovCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.jonesMarkovCoeff","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L121-L130","doc":"The **Jones-Markov coefficient** `y_λ(q) = s_{λ, X}(Q) / Z_n(Q, X)`.\n\nCombined with the Macdonald-hook telescope `Z_n = ((1−X)/(1−Q))^n`,\nthis collapses to\n\n  y_λ = Q^{n(λ)} · (1 − Q)^n / (1 − X)^n\n          · ∏_x (1 − X·Q^{c(x)}) / (1 − Q^{h(x)}). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.wenzlNormalisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.wenzlNormalisation","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L113-L117","doc":"The **Wenzl-bridge normalisation** `Z_n(Q, X)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement_nil","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L96-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.schurElement","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L65-L94","doc":"The **Wenzl Schur element** `s_{λ, X}(Q)` at partition `λ`.\n\nEncodes `Q^{n(λ)} · ∏_x (1 − X·Q^{c(x)})/(1 − Q^{h(x)})`, with\n`n(λ) = Σ_i i·λ_i` (`QPartitionCombinatorics.nLambda`).\n\n**The prefactor is `n(λ)`, NOT `contentSum`.** This read `contentSum`\n(`Σ_x (j − i)`, which is `n(λ') − n(λ)`) until 2026-08-26. The two agree\nonly for a single row of length ≤ 1 — `n([2]) = 0` against\n`contentSum [2] = 1` — and with `contentSum` the Macdonald hook telescope\n`Σ_λ f_λ·s_λ = ((1−X)/(1−Q))^n` **fails from `n = 2` upward**. Measured\nsymbolically for `n = 1..6`: exact `0` with `n(λ)`, nonzero with\n`contentSum`. The docstring was right and the code was wrong; the guard\nagainst a recurrence is `nLambda_ne_contentSum`.\n\nCross-checked against `computations/y_lambda_macdonald_telescope.py`, whose\n`schur_principal_symbolic` uses `Q ** n_lambda(p)` with\n`n_lambda(p) = Σ i·p[i]` — i.e. the Python was correct throughout and the\nLean had drifted from it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.contentSum_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.contentSum_nil","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L54-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.contentSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.contentSum","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L42-L52","doc":"The **content sum** `n(λ) = Σ_x c(x)` for partition `λ`.\n\nIterates over rows `i ∈ [0, length λ)` and within each row over\ncolumns `j ∈ [0, λ_i)`, summing `cellContent i j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.cellContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WenzlSchurElement.cellContent","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WenzlSchurElement.lean#L39-L40","doc":"Per-cell content `c(i, j) = j − i` for cell `(i, j)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}